      "description": "Sealed Classes (Java 17)"
    },
    {
      "id": "jshell-401-switch-patterns",
      "type": "CODE",
      "mode": "jshell",
      "source": "//@ anchor: switch-with-type-patterns-java-21\n//@ description: Switch with Type Patterns (Java 21)\n// --- Switch with Type Patterns (Java 21) ---\n// Type patterns in a switch, plus `when` guards for conditions the type alone\n// cannot express. The Shape hierarchy from the previous cell is still in scope.\n\nvoid classifyShape(Shape shape) {\n    String category = switch (shape) {\n        // ORDER MATTERS: cases are tested top to bottom, so the guarded case must\n        // come first. Put the unguarded `case Disc d` above it and the guarded one\n        // becomes unreachable - which the compiler will reject.\n        case Disc d when d.radius() > 10  -> \"Large disc (r=\" + d.radius() + \")\";\n        case Disc d                        -> \"Small disc  (r=\" + d.radius() + \")\";\n        case Box b when b.w() == b.h()     -> \"Square (\" + b.w() + \"x\" + b.h() + \")\";\n        case Box b                         -> \"Box (\" + b.w() + \"x\" + b.h() + \")\";\n        case Triangle t                    -> \"Triangle\";\n    };\n    System.out.println(\"  \" + category);\n}\n\nSystem.out.println(\"Shape classification:\");\njava.util.List.<Shape>of(\n    new Disc(3),\n    new Disc(15),\n    new Box(5, 5),        // matches the `when w == h` guard - a square\n    new Box(4, 7),\n    new Triangle(6, 3)\n).forEach(s -> classifyShape(s));\n\n// A RECORD PATTERN goes one step further: instead of binding the Disc and then\n// calling .radius(), it destructures the record and binds the component directly.\nShape myDisc = new Disc(7.5);\nif (myDisc instanceof Disc(double r)) {\n    System.out.printf(\"%nDisc radius via record pattern: %.1f%n\", r);\n}",
      "output": "",
      "returnValue": null,
      "executed": false,
      "executionCount": null,
      "error": "",
